#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/c9b7abb2641034c1769c6fe6b13b96edd7ccc282b61424b2031a3d37faa456e4.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/6f1bf319faf8be4a9a79c0a6f9301e6eac48a5b04f66949b679e8445b07e9d9c.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/fc1ac06787ed64ebefbb1a7a82f9bf785525777f61831bbbc39bd25c7e629d5a.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/d0249dcecf6b75cd6ff7c4623beac6fd6cfae64a58d043bb6759440167f40ea1.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f19f323-2c60-5225-b5bf-e30b8b81cb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387934} {:answer/id #uuid "c0869953-cbba-5058-a785-8f07fc88b8c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387935} {:answer/id #uuid "9e92977c-2b81-57ae-a9a4-f8a2b5d243bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387936} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fcbeb0-9818-57ae-af33-404b048bd0d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387937} {:answer/id #uuid "deefe8ad-ad6c-5901-95a4-efaef5b11775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0869953-cbba-5058-a785-8f07fc88b8c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387935} :answer-field/id #uuid "06cc8617-dfef-5744-9ccf-335b53835e97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "179abcfd-05e6-5251-a446-9e3e25a18f82" :question/math-academy-id "q-10004" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea142ec8-5dd7-5a9b-9e06-dcdb6db57742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330331} {:answer/id #uuid "25e57de6-3fc4-5fa7-af00-5f628060c8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330332} {:answer/id #uuid "df0ca58e-cc2e-51e6-91ce-63f4ad40ee6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330333} {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} {:answer/id #uuid "02238340-e005-5423-8044-8e5905140f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} :answer-field/id #uuid "247f7b3a-42e3-5c20-a1dc-8036e2c18eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f48fae54-75c1-5735-95b2-656baa979098" :question/math-academy-id "q-130562" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aa810ac-4e37-5925-aa53-4ec238a4d087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387941} {:answer/id #uuid "6472fec5-a27a-5951-84f8-172657856e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6472fec5-a27a-5951-84f8-172657856e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387942} :answer-field/id #uuid "302ec528-7e27-52a3-96f8-7310e12bba6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fae26bc2-ceda-5e9d-8e43-6adc36d30557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae26bc2-ceda-5e9d-8e43-6adc36d30557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387944} :answer-field/id #uuid "56667189-7105-5a89-bbc1-ebc527286ce2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e3804e7-9f2d-515e-94ce-3ff65ba8ead8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e3804e7-9f2d-515e-94ce-3ff65ba8ead8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387946} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fbe0f0b-d5db-5dc4-b240-c301e635fd3c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7456e1a9-a308-5389-b5cd-2f4b1bec655d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7456e1a9-a308-5389-b5cd-2f4b1bec655d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387948} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e98f0a-72bd-5167-8153-c3c07aa558fb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d7c60ce-62ca-5e1c-b6e9-61994a92ea9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316988" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $2$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $14$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $3$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-8$ | $4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-7$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+0z=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b301c4ff-2520-5ae3-9e36-9928bb586188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b301c4ff-2520-5ae3-9e36-9928bb586188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387951} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd2702dd-bdc9-5b23-b4a8-c4099afcb1cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a4c324-4d00-59e2-b3ac-570a3c85b183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58a4c324-4d00-59e2-b3ac-570a3c85b183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387953} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4c6bff3-01d0-5da6-8c8d-e674d41668fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb63a0a8-6d36-5223-aa16-a2f6ed752910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb63a0a8-6d36-5223-aa16-a2f6ed752910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387955} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a742331-8415-52ba-804c-bf79041b4014" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6224daa1-5612-55ca-9402-a871777c6579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6224daa1-5612-55ca-9402-a871777c6579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387957} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1bc8f55-70ad-5d35-aa95-f3f0ab99cbcc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abda4c5f-4458-5997-8719-4388299d2382" :question/math-academy-id "q-316995" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x=6 \\\\ 2x+z=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+0z=6 \\\\ 2x+0y+z=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ffbd0c6-7d03-5db1-969a-79c6